issue_context.body:
Hi,
I am trying to use i2c_gpio (bitbanging) on nrf52840. I am unable to make it work yet! Did anyone test bitbanging i2c on nrf52840?

Following DT settings used.
```
     gpio_i2c0: gpio_i2c {                                                                                         
         compatible = "gpio-i2c";
         status = "okay";
         clock-frequency = <I2C_BITRATE_STANDARD>;
         sda-gpios = <&gpio0 26 (GPIO_OPEN_DRAIN)>;
         scl-gpios = <&gpio0 27 (GPIO_OPEN_DRAIN)>;
         label = "GPIO_I2C_0";
         #address-cells = <1>;
         #size-cells = <0>;
     }
```

comments:
Are you trying to use I2C, or are you trying to specifically use the bit-bang I2C driver instead of the `nordic,nrf-twi` I2C device that already uses those pins?  If the latter, you need to disable the existing driver:

```
&i2c0 {
    status = "disabled";
};
```

You might also need this, or you might not.  But it was enabling input that fixed it for me.
```
     sda-gpios = <&gpio1 1 (GPIO_OPEN_DRAIN | GPIO_PULL_UP)>;
     scl-gpios = <&gpio1 2 (GPIO_OPEN_DRAIN | GPIO_PULL_UP)>;
```
